hed and line-6 not_found assertions and exact declaration-start selection without claiming test execution.","repetition":0,"result_sha256":"84f7486aa36cb0e1116ec8989040b659c7d591e5b2ea6b5e39a3cb24059223c6","sources":[{"line_end":6766,"line_start":6765,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/queries.rs","quote":"            \"mod first {\\n    fn process() { first_leaf(); }\\n}\\n\\\n             mod second {\\n    fn process() { second_leaf(); }\\n}\\n\","},{"line_end":6802,"line_start":6800,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/queries.rs","quote":"        assert!(matches!(selected.match_status, CalleesMatchStatus::Matched));\n        assert_eq!(selected.matched.unwrap().line, 5);\n        assert_eq!(selected.callees[0].name, \"second_leaf\");"},{"line_end":6817,"line_start":6809,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/queries.rs","quote":"            Some(\"modules.rs\"),\n            Some(6),\n            None,\n        )\n        .unwrap();\n        assert!(matches!(\n            wrong_line.match_status,\n            CalleesMatchStatus::NotFound\n        ));"},{"line_end":5415,"line_start":5411,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/store.rs","quote":"                 WHERE name = ?1\n                   AND (?2 IS NULL OR kind = ?2)\n                   AND (?3 IS NULL OR language = ?3)\n                   AND (?4 IS NULL OR file_path = ?4)\n                   AND (?5 IS NULL OR line_start = ?5)"}],"status":"passed"},{"answer_excerpt":"counting the embedded `modules.rs` fixture gives six input lines, with `process` declarations on lines 2 and 5. Its test source expects file alone to remain ambiguous, file plus line 5 to match, and file plus line 6 to return `not_found`","answer_sha256":"10f514ce19d60490ec314d33556cbaf012e130bd86079e36eb490835cef895f3","case":"callees-definition-boundaries-01","check":"fixture_boundary","producer_trial":"runs/callees-definition-boundaries-01-r1-bundle-boundaries","rationale":"The answer explicitly counts the encoded six-line fixture, correctly places the function declarations on lines 2 and 5, and does not describe generated line 6 as inside the second function. The frozen fixture defines the second process function entirely on generated line 5; generated line 6 closes its module. The answer accurately describes the inspected line-5 matched and line-6 not_found assertions and exact declaration-start selection without claiming test execution.","repetition":1,"result_sha256":"f2fe2e3f1ba5ad9816a6bed39c620b20f8a87ad0b728eed24159dd0300c77296","sources":[{"line_end":6766,"line_start":6765,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/queries.rs","quote":"            \"mod first {\\n    fn process() { first_leaf(); }\\n}\\n\\\n             mod second {\\n    fn process() { second_leaf(); }\\n}\\n\","},{"line_end":6802,"line_start":6800,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/queries.rs","quote":"        assert!(matches!(selected.match_status, CalleesMatchStatus::Matched));\n        assert_eq!(selected.matched.unwrap().line, 5);\n        assert_eq!(selected.callees[0].name, \"second_leaf\");"},{"line_end":6817,"line_start":6809,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/queries.rs","quote":"            Some(\"modules.rs\"),\n            Some(6),\n            None,\n        )\n        .unwrap();\n        assert!(matches!(\n            wrong_line.match_status,\n            CalleesMatchStatus::NotFound\n        ));"},{"line_end":5415,"line_start":5411,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/store.rs","quote":"                 WHERE name = ?1\n                   AND (?2 IS NULL OR kind = ?2)\n                   AND (?3 IS NULL OR language = ?3)\n                   AND (?4 IS NULL OR file_path = ?4)\n                   AND (?5 IS NULL OR line_start = ?5)"}],"status":"passed"},{"answer_excerpt":"JSDoc before scalar `const value = 1` cannot attach or carry forward to the following function.","answer_sha256":"5fcab277fa781b7147155daacc6cd035a631bb6634182f19864206407956d41e","case":"documentation-concepts-01","check":"definition_omission","producer_trial":"runs/documentation-concepts-01-r0-bundle-boundaries","rationale":"The answer describes scalar-variable documentation rejection and gives a heading contrasting absent definitions with empty fields, but does not explain that scalar initialization fails TypeScript definition extraction and therefore produces no corresponding definition or concept row. The frozen variable-declarator path calls declare_function_value; that function requires function_body_owner before push_def, and the numeric initializer reaches the None branch. Storage inserts concept rows only while iterating extracted pending symbols. Listing documentation-owner rules and saying every committed symbol receives a row does not supply this missing extraction-to-row chain.","repetition":0,"result_sha256":"7d0077dde29de642be6caf7e0079bda387da5e42d949150b3a0464d3114e38a6","sources":[{"line_end":111,"line_start":103,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer/typescript.rs","quote":"            \"variable_declarator\" => {\n                match declare_function_value(&child, source, pending, parent_index) {\n                    Some(idx) => {\n                        if let Some(value) = child.child_by_field_name(\"value\") {\n                            walk(value, source, pending, Some(idx), module_index);\n                        }\n                    }\n                    None => walk(child, source, pending, parent_index, module_index),\n                }"},{"line_end":206,"line_start":194,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer/typescript.rs","quote":"    let name_node = declarator.child_by_field_name(\"name\")?;\n    let name = node_text(&name_node, source)?.to_string();\n    let value = declarator.child_by_field_name(\"value\")?;\n    let body_owner = function_body_owner(&value)?;\n    let signature = declarator_signature(&name_node, &body_owner, source);\n    Some(push_def(\n        pending,\n        name,\n        \"function\",\n        declarator,\n        signature,\n        parent_index,\n    ))"},{"line_end":226,"line_start":209,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer/typescript.rs","quote":"fn function_body_owner<'tree>(value: &Node<'tree>) -> Option<Node<'tree>> {\n    match value.kind() {\n        \"arrow_function\" | \"function_expression\" | \"function\" => Some(*value),\n        \"call_expression\" => {\n            let args = value.child_by_field_name(\"arguments\")?;\n            let mut cursor = args.walk();\n            for arg in args.children(&mut cursor) {\n                if matches!(\n                    arg.kind(),\n                    \"arrow_function\" | \"function_expression\" | \"function\"\n                ) {\n                    return Some(arg);\n                }\n            }\n            None\n        }\n        _ => None,\n    }"},{"line_end":2462,"line_start":2460,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer.rs","quote":"             /** stalequartz ignored */\\n\\\n             const value = 1;\\n\\\n             function afterValue() {}\\n\","},{"line_end":4906,"line_start":4884,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/store.rs","quote":"            for (symbol_index, s) in pending.symbols.iter().enumerate() {\n                let parent_id = s.parent_index.map(|i| symbol_ids[i]);\n                stmt.execute(params![\n                    s.name,\n                    s.kind,\n                    &pending.path,\n                    s.line_start,\n                    s.line_end,\n                    s.signature,\n                    parent_id,\n                    language,\n                    s.decorators,\n                    production\n                ])?;\n                let symbol_id = tx.last_insert_rowid();\n                insert_concept_document(\n                    &tx,\n                    symbol_id,\n                    &s.name,\n                    &pending.path,\n                    s.signature.as_deref(),\n                    documentation_by_symbol[symbol_index].unwrap_or_default(),\n                )?;"}],"status":"failed"},{"answer_excerpt":"Blank gaps, ordinary comments, program-level file/license headers and scalar variables are rejected","answer_sha256":"b6fccd8a022ab946b5d0d63cc7467be536616a09a4873012d9506207e334a3ae","case":"documentation-concepts-01","check":"definition_omission","producer_trial":"runs/documentation-concepts-01-r1-bundle-boundaries","rationale":"The answer describes scalar-variable documentation rejection and gives a heading contrasting absent definitions with empty fields, but does not explain that scalar initialization fails TypeScript definition extraction and therefore produces no corresponding definition or concept row. The frozen variable-declarator path calls declare_function_value; that function requires function_body_owner before push_def, and the numeric initializer reaches the None branch. Storage inserts concept rows only while iterating extracted pending symbols. Listing documentation-owner rules and saying every committed symbol receives a row does not supply this missing extraction-to-row chain.","repetition":1,"result_sha256":"7f23d486c143629d85da52cf09d7b8ffbdfd5d5d6d444b7b9901d18890ce9057","sources":[{"line_end":111,"line_start":103,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer/typescript.rs","quote":"            \"variable_declarator\" => {\n                match declare_function_value(&child, source, pending, parent_index) {\n                    Some(idx) => {\n                        if let Some(value) = child.child_by_field_name(\"value\") {\n                            walk(value, source, pending, Some(idx), module_index);\n                        }\n                    }\n                    None => walk(child, source, pending, parent_index, module_index),\n                }"},{"line_end":206,"line_start":194,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer/typescript.rs","quote":"    let name_node = declarator.child_by_field_name(\"name\")?;\n    let name = node_text(&name_node, source)?.to_string();\n    let value = declarator.child_by_field_name(\"value\")?;\n    let body_owner = function_body_owner(&value)?;\n    let signature = declarator_signature(&name_node, &body_owner, source);\n    Some(push_def(\n        pending,\n        name,\n        \"function\",\n        declarator,\n        signature,\n        parent_index,\n    ))"},{"line_end":226,"line_start":209,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer/typescript.rs","quote":"fn function_body_owner<'tree>(value: &Node<'tree>) -> Option<Node<'tree>> {\n    match value.kind() {\n        \"arrow_function\" | \"function_expression\" | \"function\" => Some(*value),\n        \"call_expression\" => {\n            let args = value.child_by_field_name(\"arguments\")?;\n            let mut cursor = args.walk();\n            for arg in args.children(&mut cursor) {\n                if matches!(\n                    arg.kind(),\n                    \"arrow_function\" | \"function_expression\" | \"function\"\n                ) {\n                    return Some(arg);\n                }\n            }\n            None\n        }\n        _ => None,\n    }"},{"line_end":2462,"line_start":2460,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/indexer.rs","quote":"             /** stalequartz ignored */\\n\\\n             const value = 1;\\n\\\n             function afterValue() {}\\n\","},{"line_end":4906,"line_start":4884,"path":"mcp/servers/mmcg/src/store.rs","quote":"            for (symbol_index, s) in pending.symbols.iter().enumerate() {\n                let parent_id = s.parent_index.map(|i| symbol_ids[i]);\n                stmt.execute(params![\n                    s.name,\n                    s.kind,\n                    &pending.path,\n                    s.line_start,\n                    s.line_end,\n                    s.signature,\n                    parent_id,\n                    language,\n                    s.decorators,\n                    production\n                ])?;\n                let symbol_id = tx.last_insert_rowid();\n                insert_concept_document(\n                    &tx,\n                    symbol_id,\n                    &s.name,\n                    &pending.path,\n                    s.signature.as_deref(),\n                    documentation_by_symbol[symbol_index].unwrap_or_default(),\n                )?;"}],"status":"failed"}],"effective_results_sha256":"30e045f3fb3323fb51be951dc78ce943452b920f45f8c154e42db2e5eb05325c","human_reference":false,"kind":"mastermind-targeted-source-audit-draft","producer_input_sha256":"b48bb075606c366b3adda29ada61402f3029f5c2b97003e7973a5a37765d4b46","reviewer_kind":"agent_source_audit","schema_version":1,"scope":"two targeted defects; not a blind whole-answer grade"},"targeted_source_audit_sha256":"fded26e84b42f7ddf944c64ac01361b064ef0c0f4eb04d9417e2b560bf214e1c","unique_sessions":64}
